{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "id": "apc-mini-mk2",
  "name": "AKAI APC mini mk2",
  "notes": "APC mini mk2 (second generation). Pad grid note layout is identical to the mk1: note 0 = bottom-left, note 63 = top-right. Pads are RGB: the feedback velocity picks one of the 128 factory palette colours, and the MIDI channel of the feedback note selects brightness/behaviour (channel 1-7 = solid at 10%/25%/50%/65%/75%/90%/100% brightness, 8-11 = pulsing, 12-16 = blinking). Track buttons (notes 100-107) and scene buttons (notes 112-119) have single-colour LEDs (velocity 0 off, 1 on, 2 blinking). The shift button (note 122) has no LED. Faders (CC 48-56) are not motorized and have no LED, so fader feedback is not possible on this board.",
  "manufacturer": "AKAI Professional",
  "mode": "standard",
  "defaultMidiChannel": 1,
  "layout": {
    "width": 9,
    "height": 12
  },
